  "notes": [
    "Both annotations are model-assisted (Devin SWE-2 High sessions); they are procedurally separate reviewers, not independent human gold labels.",
    "The final label equals the adopted annotation record: annotations[0] on agreement, the adopted side for adopt-a/adopt-b, and ambiguous with the union of competing spans when unresolvable. Both annotation records with their evidence are preserved in every case.",
    "state.forcedSkillIds is admitted as evidence only for the skillCandidates signal (guide sections 2 and 3 read together); every other signal cites only its question's visible fields.",
    "Ambiguous and not_queried fields are reported outside evaluable denominators and are never converted to negative labels.",
    "Public origin is not proof that an example was absent from model training.",
    "This corpus is a practical laboratory sample: it is not statistically powered and supports no production-readiness or economy claim.",
    "Preparation made zero provider requests and selected no thresholds; the evaluation partition is locked against policy or threshold selection.",
    "Risk labels follow the guide's text-evidence rule: positive when the task text states a fact of the category (data-integrity corruption counts as data-loss, and an unconfirmed allegation still counts as textual evidence), negative when the text names no such fact; user-behavior covers surfaces the product's users or external consumers observe, not internal machinery or ops workflows. Where the frozen guide genuinely leaves a disagreement open, the label stays ambiguous per guide section 8.4 rather than revising the frozen rules."
  ]
